  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "A body of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is initially at rest. It starts moving unidirectionally under the influence of a source of constant power <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>. Its displacement in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msqrt><mi>P</mi></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>.&nbsp;The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> will be ______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Energy provided will be used to increase kinetic energy of the body. Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>P</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></msqrt><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>t</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>P</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msubsup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><msup><mi>t</mi><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mfenced><mn>0</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>16</mn><msqrt><mi>P</mi></msqrt></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>16</mn><msqrt><mi>P</mi></msqrt></math></p><p>Hence, required value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>.</p>",
